export anchor SteampunkStyle:
    number: 143
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Steampunk
    idea: A Victorian engine room on parchment, where the week reads from brass pressure gauges, projects are riveted brass plates with copper filled glass tubes, and the fortnight scrolls out of a chart recorder.
    base: light
    palette:
        parchment: #f1e6cc, the page with faint stains
        vellum: #faf3e1, ledger, tags and status pills
        brassLight: #e2c57a, plate highlight and rivet rings
        brass: #b8933f, plates and bezels, never text
        brassDeep: #6b4f16, rules, rivets and the last week line
        copper: #9a4a24, tube fluid, primary button, this week line and focus
        iron: #2e2a24, text, needles and the nav rail
        umber: #5d513f, small caps labels
        rule: #cbb98f, ledger lines
        verdigris: #2f6b5f, the On track cog and safe arc
        amber: #7d5200, At risk
        oxideRed: #9a2a1c, Behind and the pressure warning
    type:
        Display uses Playfair Display, Didot, Bodoni 72, Baskerville,
        Georgia at 700. Text uses Baskerville, Libre Baskerville, Hoefler
        Text, Garamond, Georgia. Labels are small caps tracked 0.1em.
        Greeting 42px, gauge numbers 34px with old style figures, plate
        titles 20px, body 17px at 1.5, labels 15px small caps.
    layout:
        A riveted brass plate header holds a cog emblem, Patent project
        engine over the brand, an inset vellum search, a copper pill New
        project, a round brass bell and Chief engineer Mara Okafor, over a
        dark iron nav rail with small caps links where the current one is a
        brass tab. The greeting with a long form date sits over a double
        rule, opposite a vellum Pressure warning tag. Four brass plates hold
        round gauges with cream faces, ticks, needles set to each number on
        a stated scale and a red zone for overdue, with the number below.
        The six engines are brass plates in two columns, each with category,
        name, a glass tube filled with copper to the percent, tasks, a due
        tag and a status pill. The right column holds an Engine room ledger
        with a red margin line and an Output recorder plate with a graph
        paper line chart, dashed for last week and solid copper for this.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16 to 22px inside plates, 16 to 20px between them, 28 to 32px between sections.
    density: Medium. Four gauges, six plates in two columns, a ruled ledger.
    corners: 6px plates, 3 to 4px paper, full pills on buttons and status, round gauges.
    borders: Brass bevels instead of lines, a rivet in each plate corner, double rules under the greeting, a red margin line in the ledger.
    shadows: Bevel highlights inside plates plus a soft 0 3px 6px brown drop. Fields are inset.
    icons: Engraved solid shapes in vellum pills with the small caps word. Cog On track, triangle with a bar At risk, hex nut with a bar Behind.
    focus: A 3px double copper outline offset 4px with a 2px vellum ring.
    tone: Victorian engineering labels, such as The six engines, Engine room ledger, Output recorder, Pressure warning and Chief engineer.
